#  Main Backend Components

## API Server

The API server handles:

* HTTP requests
* Assignment creation
* User operations
* Socket.IO connections
* Redis subscription


## BullMQ Worker

The worker runs separately from the API.

```text
API Container
     │
     │ Add Job
     ▼
   Redis
     │
     ▼
Worker Container
```

This separation allows the worker to be scaled independently.

---

# Assignment Creation

Example request:

```http
POST /api/assignments
```

```json
{
  "teacherId": "teacher_id",
  "title": "Operating Systems Assignment",
  "description": "Explain process scheduling algorithms",
  "dueDate": "2026-09-25"
}
```

The API:

1. Verifies the teacher.
2. Creates the assignment.
3. Adds a BullMQ job.
4. Returns the response.

Example response:

```json
{
  "message": "Assignment created successfully",
  "assignment": {
    "title": "Operating Systems Assignment",
    "description": "Explain process scheduling algorithms"
  }
}
```

---

# ⚙️ BullMQ Job Flow

A job contains data such as:

```json
{
  "assignmentId": "assignment_id",
  "teacherId": "teacher_id",
  "title": "Operating Systems Assignment"
}
```

The worker receives the job:

```text
Processing job 1
       ↓
Find students
       ↓
Create notifications
       ↓
Publish notification event
       ↓
Job completed
```

---

# 📡 Redis Pub/Sub Flow

The worker publishes:

```text
Channel:
assignment-notification
```

Example:

```json
{
  "notificationId": "notification_id",
  "studentId": "student_id",
  "assignmentId": "assignment_id",
  "message": "New assignment: Operating Systems Assignment"
}
```

The API server subscribes to the same channel.

```text
Worker
  │
  │ PUBLISH
  ▼
Redis
  │
  │ SUBSCRIBE
  ▼
API Server
```

---

# 🔔 Socket.IO Flow

When a student connects:

```text
Student
   ↓
Socket.IO
   ↓
join-user-room
   ↓
student:<studentId>
```

Example:

```javascript
socket.emit(
    "join-user-room",
    studentId
);
```

The server joins:

```javascript
socket.join(`student:${studentId}`);
```

When the notification arrives:

```javascript
io.to(`student:${studentId}`).emit(
    "new-assignment",
    data
);
```

