# 🐳 Docker Architecture

The project uses Docker Compose.

```text
                 Docker Compose
                       │
        ┌──────────────┼───────────────┐
        │              │               │
        ▼              ▼               ▼
   ┌─────────┐   ┌──────────┐   ┌──────────┐
   │   API   │   │  Worker  │   │  Redis   │
   │         │   │          │   │          │
   │ Express │   │ BullMQ   │   │ BullMQ   │
   │ Socket  │   │ Worker   │   │ Pub/Sub  │
   └────┬────┘   └────┬─────┘   └──────────┘
        │              │
        └──────────────┼──────────────┐
                       │              │
                       ▼              ▼
                  MongoDB Atlas    Redis
```

MongoDB can be hosted separately using MongoDB Atlas.

---

# 🐳 Docker Services

## API

Runs:

```bash
node src/server.js
```

## Worker

Runs:

```bash
node bullmq/notification.worker.js
```

## Redis

Runs:

```text
Redis 7
```

The API and worker communicate with Redis using:

```text
redis:6379
```

inside Docker.

---

# Running Locally Without Docker

Install dependencies:

```bash
npm install
```

Start the API:

```bash
node src/server.js
```

Start the worker separately:

```bash
node bullmq/notification.worker.js
```

Make sure Redis is running locally.

---

# Running With Docker

Build the containers:

```bash
docker compose build
```

Start:

```bash
docker compose up
```

Run in detached mode:

```bash
docker compose up -d
```

Stop:

```bash
docker compose down
```

Rebuild:

```bash
docker compose up --build
```

---

# 📊 Scaling Architecture

Suppose one teacher has 500 students.

The API should not synchronously perform all notification work.

Instead:

```text
Teacher
   ↓
API
   ↓
BullMQ
   ↓
Worker
   ↓
500 notifications
```

For larger workloads, multiple workers can process jobs:

                     BullMQ
                        │
          ┌─────────────┼─────────────┐
          ▼             ▼             ▼
      Worker 1       Worker 2      Worker 3
          │             │             │
          └─────────────┼─────────────┘
                        ▼
                     MongoDB

BullMQ supports concurrency and multiple workers, allowing background processing to scale independently from the API.


# ☁️ Deployment Architecture

The backend can be deployed using Render.

Recommended architecture:

```text
                    Internet
                       │
                       ▼
              ┌─────────────────┐
              │ Render Web      │
              │ Service         │
              │                 │
              │ Express         │
              │ Socket.IO       │
              │ Redis Subscriber│
              └────────┬────────┘
                       │
             ┌─────────┴──────────┐
             ▼                    ▼
      MongoDB Atlas          Render Redis
                                  │
                                  ▼
                         ┌─────────────────┐
                         │ Render          │
                         │ Background      │
                         │ Worker          │
                         │                 │
                         │ BullMQ          │
                         └─────────────────┘
```

The API and BullMQ worker are deployed as separate services.

